Every file borrowed from nanoVLM carries a header naming its source file. The only
changes to borrowed code are formatting (one blank line between definitions, double
quotes), added docstrings and type hints, and import paths adapted to the `tfv` package. The one
exception is a compatibility branch in tfv/models/language_model.py (marked [tinyforge-vision])
that computes the same masked causal attention on CPU/MPS, where PyTorch rejects v0.1's call;
the CUDA path is unchanged.

The MMStar evaluation (tfv/eval/) is kept logically unchanged so scores remain
comparable with the published nanoVLM-222M result (35.3%).
